{
  "title": "Internet Security Essentials: Protecting Users and Web Applications",
  "description": "A practical introduction to internet security for developers, IT staff and curious users. You will learn the goals of security and today's main threats, how HTTPS, TLS, DNS, Wi-Fi and VPNs protect (or fail to protect) data in transit, how to reason about password strength with entropy, why passkeys stop phishing, and how social engineering works. The web chapter walks through the OWASP Top 10 with runnable Node.js demonstrations of SQL injection, cross-site scripting, CSRF, password hashing with scrypt and Argon2id, secure sessions and security headers. The course closes with malware, ransomware, backups, incident response, and a hands-on review of a real web application.",
